{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"Under [Rule 6c-11](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-17/section-270.6c-11), as of November 6, 2026:\n\n- **Written policies:** Adopt and implement policies governing basket construction and acceptance, in the best interests of the ETF and its shareholders.\n- **Custom-basket parameters:** Establish detailed construction/acceptance parameters, including how parameters are revised or deviations approved.\n- **Review roles:** Specify titles or roles of investment-adviser employees required to review each custom basket for compliance with those parameters.\n- **Records:** Retain policies and, for every exchanged basket, position identifiers/descriptions (including cash), the transacting authorized participant’s identity, and—if custom—a custom designation and statement of compliance with custom-basket policies. Preserve records for at least five years, the first two easily accessible.\n- **Definition:** A custom basket contains a nonrepresentative portfolio selection, or is a representative basket differing from the initial basket used that business day.\n\n**Worth knowing:** “Non-standard order” is an operational label, not the rule’s test; unusual timing or settlement alone does not make a basket custom."}}
